+
+# Request
+
+Implement JSON Pointer (RFC 6901): export `resolvePointer(document, pointer)` from `src/index.ts`.
+It returns the value the pointer refers to, and throws when the pointer is not a valid JSON Pointer
+or does not resolve to a value of the document.
+
+# Acceptance
+
+- "" resolves to the whole document; "/" refers to the key "" .
+- `~1` decodes to `/` and `~0` to `~` (in that order); any other `~` escape is invalid.
+- A non-empty pointer must start with `/`, otherwise it throws.
+- Array indices: "0" or digits without leading zeros; "-" and out-of-range indices throw.
+- Missing keys throw; only own properties are followed (no `__proto__`, `length`, etc.).
+- Descending into a primitive or null throws.
